values ('f1c8a4d2-6b37-4e09-9a15-3d0e7c5b8f62', 'chemical-biology-and-bioorganic-chemistry', 'Chemical Biology and Bioorganic Chemistry', 'This graduate course trains students to use chemical principles, molecular design, and quantitative biological evidence to understand and control living systems. It treats chemical biology and bioorganic chemistry as a single integrated practice: mechanisms and structure-reactivity relationships are used to design probes, perturb pathways, measure biological state, and evaluate therapeutic potential. The syllabus intentionally extends topics with modern structural biology, chemical proteomics, spatial-temporal cellular control, systems chemical biology, and reproducibility standards. These additions make the course suitable for a research-intensive MS Chemistry program and for students preparing for chemical biology, medicinal chemistry, biotechnology, pharmaceutical science, or interdisciplinary life-science research.');

